\begin_layout Subsection
Local Expert Agents
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "subsec:kCELL-Context-Agents"

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
In this section,
 the tripartite structure of kCELL's local expert agents is described in detail.
 Each agent
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
\mathcal{A}_{i}=\left\{ \phi_{i},f_{i},\mathcal{M}_{i}\right\} 
\]

\end_inset

is a specialized local expert that represents its area of expertise through a smooth RBF kernel,
 maintains a local linear model and manages an internal state to track its performance.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Unlike oCELL,
 where a binary activation function is used,
 the area of expertise of local expert agents in kCELL are spatialized differently as illustrated in Figure 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "fig:Comparison-Activation-Surfaces"
plural "false"
caps "false"
noprefix "false"
nolink "false"

\end_inset

.
 A RBF kernel is used as a continuous and smooth activation function to represent the area of expertise in feature space.
 Compared to using orthotope with hard boundaries,
 this kernel-based spatialization unlocks more degrees of freedom and contributes to making the learned global function smooth and differentiable,
 making it more optimization-friendly for use control tasks.
\end_layout

