\begin_layout Definition
Forward dynamics modeling is the construction of a model that maps states (such as positions and velocities) and actions to future state trajectories.
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Definition
The learning model should learn online a data stream,
 the transition function 
\begin_inset Formula $f$
\end_inset

 of the controlled dynamical system 
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
s_{t+1}=f\left(s_{t},u_{t}\right)
\]

\end_inset

where 
\begin_inset Formula $u_{t}$
\end_inset

 is the action applied,
 
\begin_inset Formula $s_{t}$
\end_inset

 is the current state of the dynamical system and 
\begin_inset Formula $s_{t+1}$
\end_inset

 the next one.
\end_layout

