\begin_layout Standard
This chapter has defined the theoretical and algorithmic foundations of the CELL formalism.
 By detailing the iterative developemnt from the rigid spatialization of agents in oCELL to the smooth and differentiable,
 kernel-based spatialization of agents in kCELL,
 we demonstrated the modeling and adaptation capabilities of learning systems based on a self-organizing ensemble of local expert agents governed by social learning rules.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Through the experiments presented in Sections 
